#import "../lib.typ": *

#section(
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(80)

    In the author's classes the method here presented of teaching figure 3 has
    proved more satisfactory than any other that he has tested. The motion
    produces the figure; learn this motion thoroughly. Count one, two, three,
    or dot, two, three.

    #instruction[Write seventy 3's in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 7, examples: ("drill-80", "drill-80-2", "drill-80-3")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(81)

    Figure five is in a large measure dependent upon the horizontal stroke at
    the top for its legibility. This horizontal line should be made last.
    Study the form as well as practice it. Count one, two, three.

    #instruction[Write seventy 5's in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 7, examples: ("drill-81", "drill-81-2", "drill-81-3")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(82)

    Seven extends below the base. Make this figure in a count of one, two.

    #instruction[Write eighty-five 7's in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 7, examples: ("drill-82", "drill-82-2", "drill-82-3")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(83)

    Four rests on the base line, and usually the last part extends above the
    first. Count one, two, three.

    #instruction[Write sixty to seventy 4's in 60 seconds.]
  ], lines: 7, examples: ("drill-83", "drill-83-2", "drill-83-3")),
  exercise([
    #drill-heading(84)

    The compound curve at the left on the first line in drill 84, and the
    arrow in the first figure show how 8 begins.

    After a few minutes' drill on figure eight, miscellaneous figures should
    be introduced. In class work these figures should be made from the
    dictation of the teacher. The author usually makes the figures on the
    blackboard as they are dictated to the class. A fairly rapid penman can
    make from one hundred to one hundred and twenty-five of these in a minute.
    Compare your figures with the copies and make all figures small and
    disconnected.

    #instruction[Write sixty to seventy 8's in 60 seconds, then ninety to one hundred mixed figures.]
  ], lines: 7, examples: ("drill-84", "drill-84-2", "drill-84-3")),
)
